docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T12.md:12:This task creates the durable, append-only SQLite tables that back the event log: `events` for envelope rows and `event_payloads` for spilled payloads larger than the inline ceiling. It defines the migration runner that creates the schema on a fresh `.lattice/events.db`, and the indexes that make task, session, workspace, and branch scoped reads bounded. The spec requires the event log to be append-only and replayable; this task is where that invariant is encoded in the schema (no UPDATE/DELETE triggers, monotonic event_id PK). Without these tables, T13 (writer) and T14 (reader) have nowhere to land.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T12.md:16:> "Use SQLite as the durable local store unless proven insufficient. Split logical tables cleanly. Core tables: … `events`, `event_payloads`, …"
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T12.md:34:   - `events` columns: `event_id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT`, `event_uuid TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE`, `workspace_id TEXT NOT NULL`, `branch TEXT NOT NULL`, `session_id TEXT NOT NULL`, `task_id TEXT NULL`, `actor_kind TEXT NOT NULL`, `actor_detail TEXT NULL`, `kind TEXT NOT NULL`, `ts_unix_micros INTEGER NOT NULL`, `payload_hash BLOB NOT NULL`, `summary TEXT NOT NULL`, `payload_inline BLOB NULL`, `payload_spill_id INTEGER NULL`, `references_json TEXT NOT NULL`, `schema_version INTEGER NOT NULL`. Foreign key: `payload_spill_id REFERENCES event_payloads(row_id)`.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T12.md:35:   - `event_payloads` columns: `row_id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT`, `payload_hash BLOB NOT NULL UNIQUE`, `bytes BLOB NOT NULL`, `bytes_len INTEGER NOT NULL`, `created_ts_unix_micros INTEGER NOT NULL`. Content-addressed by hash so duplicate payloads dedupe naturally.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T12.md:43:   - `idx_event_payloads_hash` is the implicit UNIQUE on `payload_hash`.
