docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T14.md:12:This task exposes the read side of the event log. It defines a typed query builder for filtering by task, session, workspace, branch, kind, and time range; reconstitutes full `EventEnvelope` values (with payload inlined from either `payload_inline` or the `event_payloads` spillover join); and enforces bounded result sets so a single query can never scan the full log. The reader is the substrate that consolidation (Phase 6), verification (Phase 7), retrieval (Phase 4), and metrics (Phase 9) all sit on. Without it, the event log is write-only.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T14.md:40:6. Reconstitute payloads: for each row, if `payload_inline IS NOT NULL` deserialize from inline bytes; if `payload_spill_id IS NOT NULL` JOIN against `event_payloads` (or do a second query keyed by row_id) to load bytes. Validate the loaded bytes hash to the row's `payload_hash`; on mismatch return `EventQueryError::PayloadCorruption { event_id, expected, actual }` — never silently return the wrong payload.
