docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T76.md:1:# T76 — Phase 10 — Consolidation queue + indexing health + workspace graph health views
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T76.md:12:This task delivers the three operations-focused subviews of the review panel: the consolidation queue (background and manual-review consolidation jobs with depth/state visibility), the indexing health view (ingestion pipeline state, parser failures, vector index freshness), and the workspace graph health view (node/edge counts per family, broken-link detection, stale-edge detection). These views are how operators answer "is the daemon healthy and is its substrate trustworthy?" — without them, only the daemon-side logs show whether consolidation is keeping up, whether parsing is failing silently, or whether the graph has degenerated. Spec §10 names all three explicitly; this task delivers the last three of the eleven required operator views, completing the Phase 10 view set before smoke tests (T77).
